  "purpose": "ngspice .sens v(3) ac dec 2 1e5 1e7 (sens-ac-2.sp, at acphase=30) on a V-driven RLC ladder: dv(3)/dp per element, per m, and per AC magnitude and phase of the V card's branch drive.",
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "analytic",
    "derivation": "Nodal analysis: Y3 = m5/R5 + j w C4 mc4, ZL = j w L3, Y2 = j w C2 mc2 + 1/(ZL + 1/Y3), v3 = V/((1 + (R1/m1) Y2)(1 + ZL Y3)), V = acmag e^(j acphase pi/180), acmag = 0.042, acphase = 30 deg. Each derivative by forward-mode dual numbers over that expression (no adjoint, no finite difference); dv3/d(dc) = 0 on a linear circuit. ngspice-44.2 and ngspice-45 (stock nix builds, `ngspice -b -r`) write the same columns to 1e-6 relative on the resistors and 3e-7 on the AC phase (their forward differences) and 2e-10 elsewhere, with two ngspice defects this oracle does not inherit: both report v(r1) and v(r5) as 0 at every point after the first (their own v(r1_ac), v(r5_ac) and v(r1_m) there agree with this closed form), and a multi-point lin grid steps geometrically (cktsens.c:836-843 `inc_freq` tests LINEAR, not SENS_LINEAR), so this deck sweeps by decade."
